The memory-card save worker runs on a std::thread, which VitaSDK's pthread
creates with a 32 KiB stack. copy_stream's 64 KiB local buffer overflowed it
(V61 hardware core dump: data abort zeroing the buffer, save worker ->
open_atomic_file -> copy_stream). On the Vita only, copy in 4 KiB chunks.
Output, EOF and error semantics are unchanged; cmake/PlatformLibs.cmake gives
io.cpp TARGET_VITA=1 and fails the build if the frame grows past 8 KiB.

--- a/lib/io.cpp
+++ b/lib/io.cpp
@@ -22,7 +22,12 @@
 }
 
